sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS 4 + R1-R4 (process.stop shape: 209, @swamp/ssh, full intent as inputs). instance.create reuses this workflow for development Processes.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 1-22 (cfgmgmt file/systemd/docker_*, no shipped scripts, no report step).
  %% Decided: Nick 2026-11-02, a Docker Process runs as one plain docker run through @swamp/ssh exec; pull with cfgmgmt docker_image, check with the docker_container check. "Remove the retired unit" belongs to process:update (rule 21).
  %% Rule 23: 2026-11-03 required-only main path.
  %% status: migrated
  %% command: process:create
  %% kind: process.create
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: process:create queue<br/>--node=7 --command=…
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit process:create queue --node=7 --command=/usr/bin/php --command=artisan --command=queue:work`
  %%> - syntax: `process:create <name> (--instance=ID-or-domain | --node=ID-or-name | --project=ID --for=production) [options]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Process name, its owner (an Instance, a Node, or a Project definition) and its command
  %%> - without options: a `systemd` Process, restart policy `never`, installed and left stopped
  %%> Optional:
  %%> - `--start` starts it after it installs; see the `opt --start` blocks
  %%> - `--preset=vp-dev` (with `--instance`) adds the Vite steps
  %%> - `--runtime=docker` with `--image` runs it as a container instead of a unit; `--environment` (Docker only) adds the environment file; `--port` and `--volume` (Docker only) change only the container definition
  %%> - `--working-directory`, `--user`, `--restart`, `--keep-alive`, `--no-restart-on-deploy` change only the rendered definition
  %%> - `--idempotency-key` reuses a task start; `--json` returns JSON
  %%> Not handled here:
  %%> - a Project definition with `--for=production` is recorded only; it starts no run (R1)
  %%> - development container definitions store supported command names and resolve them when rendering; capture adopts only a compatible unlinked same-name Process, keeping its id and desired state
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, record the task<br/>Process 418: pending · #5130
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the owner's Node
  %%> - the name is free for this owner
  %%> - the `--user` account exists on the Node, from the Node agent's recorded state
  %%> - a production release directory is checked against the recorded releases, not on the Node
  %%> Result:
  %%> - Process 418 recorded with its definition, status pending
  %%> - the unit or container rendered; secret environment values pushed to the vault key `process-create-operation-5130`
  %%> - task #5130 recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-process-create
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209); every step runs there
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - `kind`: process.create
  %%> - the rendered unit, or the container definition without its environment values
  %%> - the desired state and required mounts, from recorded state
  %%> - vault key names for the environment, never the values
  %%> - the Node's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> Checked by the input schema:
  %%> - no step reads or re-checks the intent
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5130
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  opt certificate account home is not recorded
    SW->>N: Check the account<br/>ssh exec · getent
  end
  Note over SW: Prepare the definition<br/>public rendering only
  %%> Resolves the observed home in certificate paths and shapes Docker argv; no Node effects.
  opt --start
    SW->>N: Check required mounts<br/>ssh exec · stat
    %%> systemd only: each recorded required mount, or `/` when none is recorded.
  end
  opt --preset=vp-dev
    SW->>N: Publish the dev route<br/>native Vite workflow
    %%> Publishes the Vite environment before its unit starts.
  end
  SW->>N: Apply the unit<br/>cfgmgmt/systemd.apply
  %%> Publishes unitFile, reloads on content change, and applies the admitted boot and active state: stopped by default.
  opt previous activation is pending
    SW->>N: Reload systemd<br/>ssh exec · daemon-reload
    %%> Covers a prior publish that failed before daemon-reload.
  end
  SW->>N: Stop the unit<br/>ssh exec · stop
  %%> The desired state is stopped by default; cancels activating units too, which pinned apply does not stop.
  %%> With `--start` this step is skipped.
  opt --start
    opt changed unit is already running
      SW->>N: Restart if changed<br/>cfgmgmt/systemd.restart
      %%> Pinned apply leaves an already active process running after unitFile changes.
    end
  end
  SW->>N: Check the unit<br/>cfgmgmt/systemd.check
  opt --runtime=docker
    SW->>N: Pull the image<br/>cfgmgmt/docker_image
    %%> The Docker steps replace the systemd steps: the unit steps and the required-mount check are skipped.
    opt --environment
      SW->>N: Write the environment<br/>cfgmgmt/file · 0600
      %%> Docker only: the env-file for the container; vault.get content, root owner; no secret in public run data.
    end
    SW->>N: Run the container<br/>ssh exec · docker run -d
    %%> One argv command, env-file, workdir, image and exact command arguments.
    SW->>N: Stop the container<br/>ssh exec · docker stop
    %%> The detached run starts it; the desired state is stopped by default, so this step stops it.
    %%> With `--start` this step is skipped and the container keeps running.
    SW->>N: Check the container<br/>cfgmgmt/docker_container
  end
  opt --start
    opt --preset=vp-dev
      SW->>N: Check the listener<br/>ssh exec · ss
      SW->>N: Mark it awake<br/>cfgmgmt/file
    end
  end
  SW->>N: Verify it runs<br/>native assert
  %%> Requires the admitted desired state (stopped, or active with `--start`), the boot policy, and any Vite listener.
  alt desired state reached
    N-->>SW: inactive (stopped)
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the Process has its desired state: stopped
    %%> - with `--start`: active (running)
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the end check's output; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>Process 418: active
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Process 418 becomes active with its desired state
    %%> - task #5130 succeeds
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0
    %%> When:
    %%> - SSH fails, a required mount is missing, or the state does not match
    %%> How:
    %%> - the failing step ends the run with its own exit code; there is no report step
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its exit code, mapped to `error_code`
    Note over GW: Mark the Process failed<br/>task failed · rerun converges
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Process 418 is marked failed with the error code
    %%> - work done on the Node stays; nothing was copied, so nothing needs cleanup
    %%> - a new `process:update` or create converges: each behavior skips state that is already right
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5130
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
